Usage: semaphore-cli <command> [flags]

A command line interface for Semaphore operations.

Flags:
  -h, --help       Show context-sensitive help.
  -v, --version    Print the version and exit

Commands:
  evaluate [flags]
    ⚙️ Evaluate feature flags based on configuration and context

  lint [<config_file>] [flags]
    🛑 Lint Semaphore configuration file.

  generate manifest --flag_manifest_destination=STRING [flags]
    📄 (experimental) Generate an OpenFeature flag manifest based on your flags
    configuration.

  publish <dir> [flags]
    Source directory containing flags/, flagsets/ and segments/.

  publish verify [flags]
    Check the manifest and every object it lists in the bucket

  config validate <file> [flags]
    Check a bootstrap file with the loader of the relay proxy

  config print <file> [flags]
    Print the effective bootstrap file: defaults and environment overrides
    applied, secrets redacted

  segment add --segment=STRING [<id> ...] [flags]
    Add ids to the segment and bump its version key

  segment remove --segment=STRING [<id> ...] [flags]
    Remove ids from the segment and bump its version key

  segment stat --segment=STRING [flags]
    Show whether the segment exists, how many members it has, its version and
    its ttl

  segment bump --segment=STRING [flags]
    Bump the version key of the segment only, so that the relays read it again

  segment import --segment=STRING --from=STRING [flags]
    Replace the members of a segment from a file, standard input or S3, with an
    atomic swap (a temporary key, then RENAME)

  segment sync --segment=STRING --from=STRING [flags]
    Keep the segment in step with an s3 object or prefix: import it when its
    fingerprint changes

Run "semaphore-cli <command> --help" for more information on a command.
